course: dictionary
lesson: 5712
title: Longingly: wanting something very much
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When a character does something longingly, they are showing a strong wish. You can often spot it from what they look at or where they are. Think about what the character cannot have yet.
explain: Mole looks longingly towards his old home in The Wind in the Willows. He is not at home, so the way he looks shows that he misses it and wants to go back.
explain: Alice looks longingly at the lovely garden through the tiny door. She cannot get through the door, so the word tells you she wants the garden very much but cannot have it yet.
explain: Try swapping in a word you know, such as «wistfully». In the sentence «he added wistfully», it means the same as longingly: a bit sadly, and wanting something.
fact: Longingly means in a way that shows you want something very much.
fact: The wanting is often for something you cannot have.
fact: «Wistfully» means longingly, a bit sadly.
fact: Mole looks longingly towards his old home in The Wind in the Willows.
fact: Alice looks longingly at the lovely garden through the tiny door.
exercise: Mole looked longingly towards his old home. What does longingly show? | Running fast | Being angry with his home | Sleeping soundly | *Wanting something very much
exercise: Alice looks longingly at the lovely garden through the tiny door. Why does she look longingly? | *She wants the garden, but she cannot get through the door | She is cross with the door | She is fast asleep | She is bored of gardens
exercise: «...» he added wistfully. Find the word that means about the same as wistfully. | Loudly | *Longingly | Quickly | Angrily
test: The puppy looked longingly at the sausage on the plate. What is the puppy feeling? | It is tired and wants to sleep | It is happy to be fed | It is angry with the plate | *It wants the sausage very much
test: Which sentence uses longingly correctly? | *She gazed longingly at the sweets in the shop window, which she could not afford | He ran longingly to win the race | She closed the door longingly and went to bed | She laughed longingly at the funny joke
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to longingly? | Happily | *Wistfully | Loudly | Quickly
